### DeadlineRadar backend — manual test requests.
### Open in VS Code (REST Client extension) or JetBrains and click "Send Request".
### Or use the curl equivalents in README.md.

@base = http://localhost:5000

### Health check — confirms the server is up and the key is loaded
GET {{base}}/health

### Happy path — full collision payload (HIGH risk, 5h deficit)
POST {{base}}/api/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "obligations": [
    { "id": "1", "course": "CS 101", "name": "Python Homework",
      "dueDate": "2026-08-30", "type": "homework", "estimatedHours": 3, "difficulty": "medium" },
    { "id": "2", "course": "DB 201", "name": "Database Project",
      "dueDate": "2026-08-31", "type": "project", "estimatedHours": 8, "difficulty": "high" },
    { "id": "3", "course": "STAT 150", "name": "Statistics Exam",
      "dueDate": "2026-08-31", "type": "exam", "estimatedHours": 6, "difficulty": "high" }
  ],
  "availabilityPerDay": {
    "2026-08-27": 3, "2026-08-28": 3, "2026-08-29": 1, "2026-08-30": 3, "2026-08-31": 2
  },
  "riskLevel": "HIGH",
  "totalRequired": 17,
  "totalAvailable": 12,
  "hoursDeficit": 5
}

### Minimal payload — server derives riskLevel + totals itself
POST {{base}}/api/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "obligations": [
    { "course": "HIST 200", "name": "Essay draft", "dueDate": "2026-09-05", "estimatedHours": 6, "difficulty": "low" }
  ],
  "availabilityPerDay": { "2026-09-01": 3, "2026-09-02": 3, "2026-09-03": 3 }
}

### Bad request — missing obligations → 400
POST {{base}}/api/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{ "availabilityPerDay": { "2026-09-01": 3 } }
